# Public filter joint façade, ported from the b2CreateFilterJoint surface
# in joint.c. The filter joint has no anchors, no solver behaviour, and no
# tuning: every inherited query returns its base default and the constraint
# force and torque are always zero. Its only effect is the connected-joint
# collision rule: while the joint lives, the two attached bodies never form
# new contacts with each other. Contacts that already existed when the
# joint was created persist until they end naturally, exactly like
# upstream.
Class FilterJoint Inherits Joint
End Class
